<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113930" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χηρ-εύω</span></b> , intr., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be without, lack,</i> c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆσος ἀνδρῶν χ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					9.124
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Pomp.</u>
				28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				4.59
			</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ χ. τῶν ἐκπονούντων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alciphr.
					3.25
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁλκὰς τῶν ἐμπλεόντων χηρεύουσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
					1.1
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν τῆς Ἀφροδίτης ὀργίων
			χ.</span> Ach. Tat.<i><span class="en">
				4.1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδέποτε χ. τῶν ὄντων τινὸς ὁ κόσμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Herm.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				1.41.6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. ἀπό τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Steph.
					<u>in Hp.</u>
					1.219
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> abs. of a woman, <i>to
				be widowed, live in widowhood,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Is.
				6.51
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				30.11
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				33
			</span></i>; of birds, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				347
			</span></i>; also of men, <i>to be a widower,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cat.Ma.</u>
				24
			</span></i>:—
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χηρεύσῃ λέχος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					1089
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>live in solitude,</i> of a fugitive, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				479
			</span></i> (anap.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			trans., <i>bereave,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Cyc.</u>
				440
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεσὼν χηρεύσει σύνοικον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aphth.
					<u>Prog.</u>
					13
				</span></i>
			.</div>
